IMPORT `mc15-nouns`

-- Magna Carta (1215), English translation in McKechnie 1905: CHAPTERS 60 TO 63.
-- The observance of the Charter by all (60), the security of the five-and-twenty barons (61),
-- the remission of ill-will and trespasses (62) and the enjoining clause and the oath (63).
-- 61.1 (the reasons for the grant), 62.3 (the letters patent, evidence of the remission) and
-- 63.3 (the place and date of the grant) create no rule; they are listed in NOTES.md as inert,
-- reason 1, and are not quoted here.
-- Terms the text does not define, taken as plain facts: barons, the community of the whole land,
-- offence, transgression, correction, redress "as they deem fit", queen, the old relations, orders,
-- the quarrel, Easter in the sixteenth year of the reign, the restoration of peace, oath, good faith,
-- evil intent (see NOTES.md, "Terms the text does not define").
-- Dates in chapter 61 use the calendar the standard library uses; the text names no calendar.
-- GENERATED from tools/templates/mc15-ch60-63.l4.in by tools/build.py; edit the template.

§ `Chapters 60 to 63 -- observance, the security of the barons, remission and the oath`

§§ `Chapter 60 -- the observance of the customs and liberties by all`

-- src:127 | Moreover, all the aforesaid customs and liberties, the observance of which we have granted in our kingdom as far as pertains to us towards our men, shall be observed by all of our kingdom, as well clergy as laymen, as far as pertains to them towards their men.
@ref Chapter 60 (src:127)
GIVEN `the person is of the kingdom, clergy or lay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has men` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 60 -- the person must observe the customs and liberties towards his men` IS
    IF `the person is of the kingdom, clergy or lay`
    THEN IF `the person has men`
         THEN Obliged
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "as far as pertains to them towards their men" limits the duty to what they owe their men; it does not say that one with no men owes nothing (F64c).
         ELSE `Obligation not covered`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Obligation not covered`

-- src:127 | Moreover, all the aforesaid customs and liberties, the observance of which we have granted in our kingdom as far as pertains to us towards our men, shall be observed by all of our kingdom, as well clergy as laymen, as far as pertains to them towards their men.
@ref Chapter 60 (src:127)
GIVEN `the person is of the kingdom, clergy or lay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has men` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 60 -- the customs and liberties shall be observed by all of our kingdom towards their men` IS
    IF `ch 60 -- the person must observe the customs and liberties towards his men` `the person is of the kingdom, clergy or lay` `the person has men` EQUALS Obliged
    THEN PARTY `a member of the kingdom, clergy or lay`
         MUST `observe towards his men the customs and liberties which the King has granted towards his men`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `a member of the kingdom, clergy or lay` BECAUSE "ch 60: a member of the kingdom did not observe the customs and liberties towards his men"
    ELSE FULFILLED

